{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7KtCNxcCywDeGAh2GDy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Before I draft, one thing you should know: your own numbers don't back up \"every charter boat will go out of business.\" In 2016 your bookings fell 19% and came back to 155 within two years. The commission staff may well know that history. If you open with a claim they can disprove, they may stop listening to the rest of your two minutes. Your strongest case is that the cut hits charters hard while charters land only 9% of the fish. That case gets stronger if you can show what lost trips actually cost.\n\nThese answers would change what I write:\n\n1. **What do you want the commission to do instead?** For example: keep 4, settle on 3, give charter boats a separate limit, make the cut shorter than 3 years, or use a size limit or season change instead. Asking for something specific usually lands better than a flat no.\n2. **How many trips can you lose before you stop making money?** What does a season cost you to run (fuel, slip, insurance, crew, boat payments)? If you went from 160 trips to 130 and that wipes out your profit, that's what makes \"out of business\" believable.\n3. **What happened to the other boats after 2016?** Did any of the 11 (or the boats there then) close, sell, or cut back? Did the bounce back to 155 happen for other reasons, like the limit going back up or prices rising?\n4. **More on the survey:** what did the other 17 of the 70 say? Did anyone say how many fewer trips they'd book? How were the 70 picked? The commission will ask whether it's a fair sample.\n5. **Who else depends on these trips?** For example, deckhands, tackle shops, marinas, motels and restaurants. Rough numbers are fine.\n6. **For the opening line:** what's your name, your boat's name, the harbor, and do you speak for the charter association or just yourself?\n\nAnd one open question: is there anything else the commission knows or will find out that cuts against you? For example, charter landings going over a past target, catches already dropping, or the association backing an earlier cut.\n\nIf you don't know some of these, tell me and I'll write without them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":617,"cache_read_input_tokens":9584,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":617},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ab5cd844-d348-4e3e-a219-34f2d79b1245","uuid":"a93048b0-7e13-4ec1-9628-1b6393e888f2","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:35:45.327Z","request_id":"req_011Ch7KtCBK6T4oW5HCcv2E1"}
